See the total profit and cost of treaties before you sign them (including shipping lanes), and get smart default quantities with [b]Smart Treaties mod[/b].

No more hidden bad deals where you lose thousands a week without realizing it, and no more clicking around to get the right quantity.

[h2]Predicted net profit or loss before you sign[/h2]

[list]
[*][b]Predicted profit on every good.[/b] Each card in the goods picker shows its best weekly profit in green, so you see which goods are worth sending before you click one.
[*][b]A smart default quantity.[/b] Picking a good starts at its most profitable quantity, instead of the game's 25% default.
[*][b]Three buttons under the slider.[/b] [b]Best[/b]: the most profit while your partner still accepts the good. [b]Max[/b]: fills their shortage without going over your surplus. [b]👍[/b]: the highest acceptance, at the lowest cost.
[*][b]Net profit and cost under the slider[/b], live as you move it. Hover it for sale, purchase and shipping cost (no shipping cost when your markets border each other).
[/list]

[h2]Real net profit or loss on all your treaties after you sign[/h2]

[list]
[*][b]Net per treaty[/b] in the outliner, with the total on the Treaties header.
[*][b]Net per good[/b] in the treaty panel. Hover for the full breakdown, shipping lane cost included.
[*][b]Net treaty income[/b] in the treasury tooltip, next to the game's own revenue and expenses (no need to hover on 3 different areas to see if your treaties lose money).
[/list]

[h2]Where the numbers come from[/h2]

Predicted prices use the game's own price rule, at first-week prices. Signed treaties use the real buying / selling / shipping lane costs. A draft has no route yet (the game only picks one when you sign), so drafts assume a medium-length route (we use the real costs once it's signed).

[h2]No cheating[/h2]

Display only. The buttons set the slider, exactly as you would by hand. Nothing changes your economy, your treaties or the AI.

[h2]Compatibility[/h2]

[list]
[*][b]Game version 1.13.[/b]
[*][b]Achievement compatible.[/b]
[*][b]Save-safe.[/b] Add or remove it mid-campaign; it stores nothing in your save.
[*][b]Single-player.[/b] The treaty totals assume one human player.
[*][b]All eleven languages Victoria 3 ships:[/b] English, Français, Deutsch, Español, Português do Brasil, Polski, Русский, 简体中文, 日本語, 한국어, Türkçe. Terms come from the game's own text, but these are not native-speaker translations. Post a correction and it goes in.
[*][b]Conflicts:[/b] it replaces the goods transfer picker, the treaty article and influence cells, the outliner's treaty rows, and two lines of the treasury tooltip. Another mod changing those same pieces will clash.
[/list]

[h2]Feedback[/h2]
Share any issues in this thread and I will fix it. Suggestions and ratings welcome too !
